  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "If Casey were to give David $\\$3$, then they would have the same amount of money. On the other hand, if Casey were to give David $\\$12$, then David would have three times as much money as Casey. How much money do they each have?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Casey has $\\$21$ and David has $\\$15$.\n\nModel both transfers with simultaneous equations and solve by substitution.",
      "worked": "Let Casey have $x$ dollars and David have $y$ dollars originally.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x-3&=y+3\\\\x&=y+6\\\\y+12&=3(x-12)\\\\y+12&=3(y+6-12)\\\\y+12&=3y-18\\\\30&=2y\\\\y&=15\\\\x&=15+6\\\\x&=21\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, Casey has $\\$21$ and David has $\\$15$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 92
  },
